### [02:22:10 UTC] Step 1 — Exercise read_audio/write_audio on synthesized sample
Input: fat_llama/audio_fattener/feed.py read_audio/write_audio; synthesized 1s 440 Hz Sine mp3 (pydub.generators.Sine pattern from test_feed.py).
Action: Wrote+ran scratchpad/step1_rw.py under .venv/Scripts/python.exe; inspected output with soundfile.info/read and mutagen.flac.FLAC; measured dominant frequency and tone purity in/out; also exercised the 'wav' branch.
Reasoning: Need measured bitrate/sample-rate/channel/duration properties plus content sanity before scoring anything.
Output: Input mp3 -> sr=44100, mono, 1000ms, bitrate=63999, samples on raw PCM scale (min -31212, max 31145, rms 22011).
Output flac -> sr=44100 (preserved), channels=1 (preserved), duration=1.0s (matches), subtype PCM_24, flac bitrate 938384 bps, no NaN/Inf.
FAIL: clipped_fraction = 0.99993 (99.99% of samples at full scale); data_rms=0.99997. tone_purity 0.99999 in -> 0.81066 out (= 8/pi^2, the exact square-wave fundamental fraction) => sine was squared off. Same for the 'wav' branch (clipped 0.99993). Dominant freq 440 Hz preserved in both.
Root cause: read_audio returns raw integer-PCM-scale float64; write_audio passes it straight to sf.write(..., subtype='PCM_24'), and soundfile interprets float input as [-1,1] full scale, clamping everything.

